Clean flat 2D vector technical illustration for an open-source Go infrastructure project. A calm, sparse left-to-right dependency graph: six or seven simple rounded-rectangle module nodes of modest varying sizes, aligned on a quiet grid, joined by thin precise straight connector lines. Flat matte fills with subtle thin borders; connectors thin and straight. Generous negative space and breathing room — elements occupy a central horizontal band with large empty margins on every side; do not fill the frame. Strict restricted palette: solid matte background exactly deep slate ink #0F172A; nodes and lines in slate gray #334155 and lighter #94A3B8; exactly one node and exactly one connector edge in a single restrained muted teal #2DD4BF, with no other use of teal or any other color. Pure flat vector aesthetic, no gradients, no shadows, no 3D, no bevels, no gloss, no reflections, no texture, no lighting. The visual restraint of Go language branding, Tailwind docs, Linear, and fly.io. Abstract modules only: no icons, no symbols, no labels, no text, no numbers, no logos, no people, no UI screenshots. Precise geometry, crisp edges, sparse, technical, anti-hype.
